{
  "format": 1,
  "about": "ASoftware setup: what every installer (PC: Install-ASoftware.ps1, ios26/Install-iOS26.ps1, watchos/Install-watchOS.ps1, Setup-ASoftware.ps1; phone: the Android app's own setup) downloads from Apple and which steps it runs. Draft 2026-11-08 by the phone-setup session, filled from the scripts in ios-sweet-watch (branch watchos-installer) and from the IPSWs' own central directories (crc32, zipBytes, method). bytes = the member's size once unpacked (what the installers pin today); zipBytes = its size inside the zip when deflated (method 8). GB = 10^9. Since 2026-11-08 (phone-steps / phone-ios26): the Linux step bodies of ios26/Install-iOS26.ps1 and watchos/Install-watchOS.ps1 are files, ios26/steps/NAME.sh and watchos/steps/NAME.sh of asoft-ios, which both PC installers (Step-Body) and the phone's setup read; their {PLACEHOLDERS} come from each OS's vars here. os.*.steps lists the PC steps, each Linux body with the disks (ro/rw/new; at = where the body finds it; overlay = the qcow2 it is made on first), the files in and the files out of its helper-VM run (Run-Linux's -Disks/-In/-Out).",
  "helper": {
    "files": [
      "installer/helper/out/Image.gz",
      "installer/helper/out/initrd.gz"
    ],
    "machine": "-M virt -cpu cortex-a76 -m 4G, virtio-blk disks found by serial",
    "jobs": {
      "build-root": "disks ipsw (ro), root (16 GiB), scratch (10 GiB qcow2): iOS 16's root disk from its IPSW",
      "run": "disks in (tar: .job/run, .job/disks, .job/out), out (the result as a tar), and the job's own: the iOS 26 / watchOS installers' Linux steps",
      "selftest": "tools and the ipsw disk"
    }
  },
  "shared": {
    "title": "What iOS 26 and watchOS share: cloudOS 26.4b's research kernel, SPTM, TXM, device tree and ramdisk, darwin-vm's sysroot and the guest GPU driver (downloaded once, for either)",
    "sources": {
      "cloudos": {
        "url": "https://updates.cdn-apple.com/private-cloud-compute/c0ecdb4b310cf5239ab2b248dd3098eec297dc5aa3bbe6ada27273262b0b8b64",
        "members": [
          {
            "name": "kernelcache.research.vphone600",
            "role": "kernel"
          },
          {
            "name": "Firmware/sptm.vresearch1.release.im4p",
            "role": "sptm"
          },
          {
            "name": "Firmware/txm.iphoneos.research.im4p",
            "role": "txm"
          },
          {
            "name": "Firmware/all_flash/DeviceTree.vphone600ap.im4p",
            "role": "devicetree"
          },
          {
            "name": "094-39914-031.dmg",
            "role": "ramdisk"
          },
          {
            "name": "Firmware/094-39914-031.dmg.trustcache",
            "role": "ramdisk-trustcache"
          },
          {
            "name": "094-39278-029.dmg.aea",
            "role": "gpu-image",
            "note": "the cloudOS OS image, only for the guest GPU driver (its AEA key is in its own header); deleted once the driver is out"
          },
          {
            "name": "Firmware/094-39278-029.dmg.aea.trustcache",
            "role": "gpu-image-trustcache"
          }
        ],
        "note": "sizes and CRCs are the zip's own (IpswFetch checks them); the release kernelcache is not needed on the phone"
      }
    },
    "files": {
      "sysroot": {
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jprx/darwin-vm/edfc19433da8d04d5927a7b1932acce4034f307c/sysroot/ios_sysroot.tar.gz",
        "sha256": "EE27653106055A6046428465D1CF68F5DFDC1BE5E9B6FFDF402BDD0B6034A8DC"
      },
      "dtFixup": {
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alpersamur3/qemu-sptm/52f360682d261c03b3db94ced1ce1c8303a96478/scripts/darwin/vresearch_dt_fixup.py",
        "sha256": "6DE7F5834430322DCBC0D7C09D99AE9B9D7E0A1E1F9C307CC3FF302FCCE5E608"
      },
      "gpuPlugin": {
        "name": "libAppleParavirtCompilerPluginIOGPUFamily.dylib",
        "url": "https://github.com/alpersamur3/asoft-ios/releases/download/graphicloader-9cadb5c/libAppleParavirtCompilerPluginIOGPUFamily.dylib",
        "sha256": "089E725E7733B0B84F5F7821E80DF4E7FC12BD876DD84D753493FA51BD57B8A5"
      },
      "fcsKeys": {
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/blacktop/ipsw/v3.1.739/pkg/aea/data/fcs-keys.gz",
        "sha256": "5632BD384FCF07F107066DC1360804343EAA3510DE0F408ED0A1888D480F30EA",
        "note": "the FCS private keys blacktop/ipsw 3.1.739 carries (the PC installers decrypt with that ipsw); the phone asks Apple's key service first and takes a key from this list when it does not answer"
      }
    },
    "vars": {
      "RAMDISK": "094-39914-031.dmg",
      "IMG": "094-39278-029.dmg",
      "BUNDLE": "AppleParavirtGPUMetalIOGPUFamily.bundle",
      "PLUGIN": "libAppleParavirtCompilerPluginIOGPUFamily.dylib"
    },
    "base": {
      "steps": [
        "setup",
        "prereq",
        "python",
        "qemu",
        "linux",
        "sysroot",
        "cloudos",
        "firmware",
        "devicetree",
        "ramdisk",
        "gpudriver"
      ],
      "note": "Install-iOS26.ps1 -Base runs only these: all watchOS needs from iOS 26. iOS 26 can follow on the same work folder. -Base leaves out kernelcache.release.vphone600 (as the phone does), takes GpuMode cloudos when none is chosen and stops on gpuless. Install-watchOS.ps1's check step runs it when its work folder has no base."
    }
  },
